  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#infrastructure defines a number of terms that are defined in other specs by pointing at these specs.\n\nThis double definition gets picked up by the definition database that backs up respec and bikeshed, which makes at least bikeshed (and probably respec, but I don't use it) confued as to which spec you're trying to link to when using one of these terms. For instance, I'm using `px` in the mediaqueries spec, and bikeshed complains:\n\n> LINK ERROR: Multiple possible 'maybe' refs for 'px'.\n> Arbitrarily chose the one in html.\n> If this is wrong, insert one of the following lines into a &lt;pre class=link-defaults> block:\n> spec:css-values-4; type:value; text:px\n> spec:html; type:value; text:px\n\nSince the html definition is merely a pointer to the css one, this isn't helping.\n\nMaybe these redirecting definitions be changed so that they're only valid within the html spec, so that other specs attempting to use these terms can directly (and automatically) point to their primary definitions?\n\nCCing @tabatkins in case this is a problem with the tooling rather than one with the way the spec is written.\n",
